{
  "tema": 8528,
  "slug": "contar-significados",
  "titulo": "Different meanings of the verb contar",
  "subtitulo": "Contar ovejas, contar un chisme, eso no cuenta, cuenta conmigo.",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "Contar = to count (numbers, things), to tell (a story, news), to count / matter (eso no cuenta), and contar con = to count on, to have.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Contar** (o > ue: **cuento**, **cuentas**) has several meanings depending on the context:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Meaning",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "_to count_ (numbers, things)",
              "Voy a contar las monedas."
            ],
            [
              "_to tell, to narrate_",
              "Mi papá me contó un chisme."
            ],
            [
              "_to count, to matter_",
              "Ese examen no cuenta."
            ],
            [
              "contar con: _to count on, to rely on_",
              "Cuenta conmigo."
            ],
            [
              "contar con: _to have, to feature_",
              "El hotel cuenta con alberca."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "For _to count_ and _to tell_ it's transitive: no preposition before the object (**cuenta las monedas**, **cuenta mentiras**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: you count coins, you tell stories, and you can always count **con** your friends."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿Ya sabes ==contar== del uno al cincuenta?",
              "en": "Can you count from one to fifty yet?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Para dormirte, ==cuenta== borreguitos.",
              "en": "To fall asleep, count sheep."
            },
            {
              "es": "Beto siempre ==cuenta== mentiras.",
              "en": "Beto always tells lies."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ayer mi papá me ==contó== que la vecina tiene novio.",
              "en": "Yesterday my dad told me the neighbor has a boyfriend."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Es cierto que te mudas? —No, ¿quién te ==contó== eso?",
              "en": "\"Is it true you're moving?\" \"No, who told you that?\""
            },
            {
              "es": "Este examen no ==cuenta== para la calificación final.",
              "en": "This exam doesn't count toward the final grade."
            },
            {
              "es": "Si necesitas ayuda, ==cuenta conmigo==.",
              "en": "If you need help, count on me."
            },
            {
              "es": "El hotel ==cuenta con== alberca y gimnasio.",
              "en": "The hotel has a pool and a gym."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
